    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816344\">@Aaron Liu</span> Do you think that the <code>termination_by</code> hints are correct, semantically speaking? That is, <code>getSize</code> does reduce at every recursive call?</p>",
        "id": 597315195,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1779548601
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yes, it seems to be reducing</p>",
        "id": 597315358,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779548749
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmmm.... but then shouldn't the goals be provable? Or, am I missing something?</p>",
        "id": 597315429,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1779548799
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>no, one of the goals isn't provable, because it requires reasoning about the value of <code>bar []</code></p>",
        "id": 597315498,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779548850
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh, don't we get that from the definition of <code>bar</code>? Or is that not accessible while inside the <code>mutual</code> block?</p>",
        "id": 597315596,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1779548910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it's not accessible from within the termination proof</p>",
        "id": 597315618,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779548943
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816344\">@Aaron Liu</span>  Oh, ok.... Thanks <span aria-label=\"+1\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"+1\">:+1:</span></p>",
        "id": 597315674,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1779548987
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interestingly enough, unfolding in the termination proof is actually perfectly sound (as long as you're not unfolding the function you're in). I recently actually made a prototype of this and just added your example <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/Rob23oba/332ae7453616fc12e3f62f9e29ee0001\">here</a>. I might also try to develop onto it to make a more powerful mutual but no promises.</p>",
        "id": 597405713,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1779634490
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"873547\">@Robin Arnez</span> Oh, wow! That's really interesting... Thanks a lot!</p>",
        "id": 597465570,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1779683611
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873547\">Robin Arnez</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Termination.20proof.20for.20mutually.20recursive.20definitions/near/597405713\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Interestingly enough, unfolding in the termination proof is actually perfectly sound (as long as you're not unfolding the function you're in). I recently actually made a prototype of this and just added your example <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/Rob23oba/332ae7453616fc12e3f62f9e29ee0001\">here</a>. I might also try to develop onto it to make a more powerful mutual but no promises.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Even though <code>WellFounded.fix</code> is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Init/WF.html#WellFounded.fix\">marked <code>noncomputable</code></a>,  <code>natFixHelper</code> in your code is not. Could you explain how that works?</p>\n<p>Actually I was trying to emulate your code to fit my use-case, and was getting stuck.</p>",
        "id": 605709400,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1782132846
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFounded.fix_eq_fixC#doc\">docs#WellFounded.fix_eq_fixC</a> is a <code>csimp</code> lemma that causes the compiler to translate every instance of the noncomputable <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFounded.fix#doc\">docs#WellFounded.fix</a> into the computable <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=WellFounded.fixC#doc\">docs#WellFounded.fixC</a>. But I don't know whether it works well as an efficient implementation...</p>",
        "id": 605811603,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1782151127
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"873547\">@Robin Arnez</span> Thanks a lot! <span aria-label=\"grinning\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f600\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning\">:grinning:</span></p>",
        "id": 605905518,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1782188450
    }
]